# Fingerprints of reviewed false positives.
#
# `gitleaks detect` scans the diff of every commit in the range, so a finding
# introduced by an earlier commit stays reported no matter what later commits
# do — an inline `gitleaks:allow` added afterwards cannot reach back and change
# that commit's diff. Fingerprints are the mechanism for exactly this case.
#
# Add an entry only with a one-line justification. Never add a real secret here:
# if a credential was committed, rotate it — an ignore rule does not un-publish
# anything.

# FastAPI's openapi_url parameter. generic-api-key fires on the parameter name
# containing "api" beside a string literal; the value is the route path
# /api/v1/openapi.json, not a credential. Verified against a fixture containing
# real randomly-generated secrets — those are still reported.
